From: N0zoM1z0 <161784452+N0zoM1z0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:49:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Define the data of Rika's, Meira's and the dialog TUs in C++

The dialog face tables were local initializers in the original: their
anonymous data appears in function order, and only word-element tables
are word-aligned (-a2), so the byte tables are plain arrays rather than
Array structs. Array's storage is public so that it can be brace-
initialized.
---
 platform/array.hpp          |   2 +-
 th02/dialog.cpp             |   2 +-
 th02/main/boss/meira.cpp    |  12 +-
 th02/main/boss/rika.cpp     |   9 +-
 th02/main/dialog/dialog.cpp | 168 ++++++++++++++-----
 th02/shiftjis/main.hpp      |  13 ++
 th02_main.asm               | 323 ------------------------------------
 7 files changed, 149 insertions(+), 380 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/array.hpp b/platform/array.hpp
index 10e0c2e2..5e41d623 100644
--- a/platform/array.hpp
+++ b/platform/array.hpp
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ template <class T, size_t N> using Array = std::array<T, N>;
 template <class T, int N> struct Array {
 	typedef int size_type;
 
-private:
+	// Public, so that it can be brace-initialized like ZUN's local arrays.
 	T v[N];
 
 public:
